sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: To find the sixth binomial line.
----
proof:

Set out two numbers {AC} and {CB} such that {AB} does not have to either of them the ratio which a square number has to a square number, and let there also be another number {D} which is not square and which does not have to either of the numbers {BA} or {AC} the ratio which a square number has to a square number.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="160" height="270" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="X.53 diagram" src="propX53.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    // Joyce's figure: the number AB (blue) with C on it, the number D
    // (blue), the rational line E, and FH with G on it. Added, all hidden at
    // rest: transparent targets AC, CB (;0;0;0); solid twins FG, GH
    // (initiallyHidden) so each term strokes in as it is contrived. K, the
    // line whose square makes up the excess, is not drawn in Joyce's figure
    // and stays literal; "commensurable in length with A" is his slip for K
    // and is left literal too.
    //
    // Draggables (checked against the bundle): A, B, C (the numbers AC, CB),
    // D1, D2 (the number D), E1, E2 (the line E), F, and the offscreen
    // frees. D1/D2, E1/E2 and F arrive with "another number D", "set out any
    // rational straight line E" and "the square on FG", so they are deferred.
    // G and H are derived (meanProportional) and listed per slide.
    var GIVEN = ["A","B","C","AB","AC","CB"];
    var NUMD  = GIVEN.concat(["D","D1","D2"]);
    var RAT   = NUMD.concat(["E","E1","E2"]);
    var TFG   = RAT.concat(["F","G","FG"]);
    var TGH   = TFG.concat(["H","GH"]);
    var ALL   = TGH.concat(["FH"]);
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "canvas_0",
        background: "35,19,100",
        title: "X.53",
        elements: [
            "A0;point;free;40,-1000;0;0",
            "A3;point;free;40,1000;0;0",
            "D0;point;free;70,-1000;0;0",
            "D3;point;free;70,1000;0;0",
            "E0;point;free;100,-1000;0;0",
            "E3;point;free;100,1000;0;0",
            "F0;point;free;130,-1000;0;0",
            "F3;point;free;130,1000;0;0",
            "A;point;lineSlider;A0,A3,0,30",
            "B;point;lineSlider;A0,A3,0,220",
            "C;point;lineSlider;A0,A3,0,150",
            "AB;line;connect;A,B;0;0;blue",
            "D1;point;lineSlider;D0,D3,0,30;0",
            "D2;point;lineSlider;D0,D3,0,125;0",
            "D;line;connect;D1,D2;black;0;blue",
            "E1;point;lineSlider;E0,E3,0,30;0",
            "E2;point;lineSlider;E0,E3,0,110;0",
            "E;line;connect;E1,E2;black",
            "F;point;lineSlider;F0,F3,0,30",
            "G';point;proportion;D1,D2,A,B,E1,E2,F,F3;0;0",
            "G;point;meanProportional;E1,E2,F,G',F,F3",
            "H';point;proportion;B,A,A,C,F,G,G,F3;0;0",
            "H;point;meanProportional;F,G,G,H',G,F3",
            "FH;line;connect;F,H",
            // Slide-only twins and highlight targets.
            "AC;line;connect;A,C;0;0;0",
            "CB;line;connect;C,B;0;0;0",
            "FG;line;connect;F,G",
            "GH;line;connect;G,H"
        ],
        initiallyHidden: ["FG","GH"],
        deferDraggables: ["D1","D2","E1","E2","F"],
        aliases: { "BA": "AB", "BC": "CB", "HG": "GH" },
        slides: [
            { text: "“To find the sixth binomial line.”",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["FH"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "X.53" }] },
            { text: "Set out two numbers {AC} and {CB}",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["AC","CB"] },
            { text: "such that {AB} does not have to either of them the ratio which a square number has to a square number,",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["AB"] },
            { text: "and let there also be another number {D} which is not square",
              visible: NUMD,
              highlighted: ["D"] },
            { text: "and which does not have to either of the numbers {BA} or {AC}",
              visible: NUMD,
              highlighted: ["D","AB","AC"] },
            { text: "the ratio which a square number has to a square number.",
              visible: NUMD,
              highlighted: ["D","AB","AC"] },
            { text: "Set out any rational straight line {E},",
              visible: RAT,
              highlighted: ["E"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "E", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect } ] } },
            { text: "and let it be contrived that {D} is to {AB} as the square on {E} is to the square on {FG}.",
              visible: TFG,
              highlighted: ["D","AB","E","FG"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "F",  name: geomlib.A.Point.appear },
                  { elem: "FG", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "D : AB = E² : FG²", ref: "X.6.Cor" }] },
            { text: "Then the square on {E} is commensurable with the square on {FG}.",
              visible: TFG,
              highlighted: ["E","FG"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "X.6" }] },
            { text: "And {E} is rational, therefore {FG} is also rational.",
              visible: TFG,
              highlighted: ["E","FG"] },
            { text: "Now, since {D} does not have to {AB} the ratio which a square number has to a square number,",
              visible: TFG,
              highlighted: ["D","AB"] },
            { text: "neither does the square on {E} have to the square on {FG}",
              visible: TFG,
              highlighted: ["E","FG"] },
            { text: "the ratio which a square number has to a square number,",
              visible: TFG,
              highlighted: ["E","FG"] },
            { text: "therefore {E} is incommensurable in length with {FG}.",
              visible: TFG,
              highlighted: ["E","FG"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "E, FG incommensurable in length", ref: "X.9" }] },
            { text: "Again, let it be contrived that {BA} is to {AC} as the square on {FG} is to the square on {GH}.",
              visible: TGH,
              highlighted: ["AB","AC","FG","GH"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "GH", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "H",  name: geomlib.A.Point.appear } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "BA : AC = FG² : GH²", ref: "X.6.Cor" }] },
            { text: "Then the square on {FG} is commensurable with the square on {HG}.",
              visible: TGH,
              highlighted: ["FG","GH"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "X.6" }] },
            { text: "Therefore the square on {HG} is rational. Therefore {HG} is rational.",
              visible: TGH,
              highlighted: ["GH"] },
            { text: "And, since {BA} does not have to {AC} the ratio which a square number has to a square number,",
              visible: TGH,
              highlighted: ["AB","AC"] },
            { text: "neither does the square on {FG} have to the square on {GH}",
              visible: TGH,
              highlighted: ["FG","GH"] },
            { text: "the ratio which a square number has to a square number,",
              visible: TGH,
              highlighted: ["FG","GH"] },
            { text: "therefore {FG} is incommensurable in length with {GH}.",
              visible: TGH,
              highlighted: ["FG","GH"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "FG, GH incommensurable in length", ref: "X.9" }] },
            { text: "Therefore {FG} and {GH} are rational straight lines commensurable in square only.",
              visible: TGH,
              highlighted: ["FG","GH"] },
            { text: "Therefore {FH} is binomial.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["FH"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "FH binomial", ref: "X.36" }] },
            { text: "It is next to be proved that it is also a sixth binomial straight line.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["FH"] },
            { text: "Since {D} is to {AB} as the square on {E} is to the square on {FG},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["D","AB","E","FG"] },
            { text: "and also {BA} is to {AC} as the square on {FG} is to the square on {GH},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AB","AC","FG","GH"] },
            { text: "therefore, ex aequali, {D} is to {AC} as the square on {E} is to the square on {GH}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["D","AC","E","GH"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "D : AC = E² : GH²", ref: "V.22" }] },
            { text: "But {D} does not have to {AC} the ratio which a square number has to a square number,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["D","AC"] },
            { text: "therefore neither does the square on {E} have to the square on {GH}",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["E","GH"] },
            { text: "the ratio which a square number has to a square number,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["E","GH"] },
            { text: "therefore {E} is incommensurable in length with {GH}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["E","GH"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "E, GH incommensurable in length", ref: "X.9" }] },
            { text: "But it was also proved incommensurable with {FG},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["E","FG"] },
            { text: "therefore each of the straight lines {FG} and {GH} is incommensurable in length with {E}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["FG","GH","E"] },
            { text: "And, since {BA} is to {AC} as the square on {FG} is to the square on {GH},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AB","AC","FG","GH"] },
            { text: "therefore the square on {FG} is greater than the square on {GH}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["FG","GH"] },
            { text: "Let then the sum of the squares on {GH} and K equal the square on {FG}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["GH","FG"] },
            { text: "Then, in conversion, {AB} is to {BC} as the square on {FG} is to the square on K.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AB","CB","FG"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "AB : BC = FG² : K²", ref: "V.19.Cor" }] },
            { text: "But {AB} does not have to {BC} the ratio which a square number has to a square number,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AB","CB"] },
            { text: "so that neither does the square on {FG} have to the square on K",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["FG"] },
            { text: "the ratio which a square number has to a square number.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["FG"] },
            { text: "Therefore {FG} is incommensurable in length with A.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["FG"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "X.9" }] },
            { text: "Therefore the square on {FG} is greater than the square on {GH}",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["FG","GH"] },
            { text: "by the square on a straight line incommensurable with {FG}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["FG"] },
            { text: "And {FG} and {GH} are rational straight lines commensurable in square only,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["FG","GH"] },
            { text: "and neither of them is commensurable in length with the rational straight line {E} set out.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["FG","GH","E"] },
            { text: "Therefore {FH} is a sixth binomial straight line.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["FH"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "Q.E.D." }] }
        ],
        resolveJustification: function(ref) {
            if (ref === "X.53") return "#prop";
            return (window.eucrefs && window.eucrefs[ref]) || null;
        }
    });

    // Per-page citation lookup for the slideshow's resolveJustification.
    window.eucrefs = (window.eucrefs || {});
    Object.assign(window.eucrefs, {
        "V.19.Cor":   "/elements/books/bookV/propositions/propV19/#cor",
        "V.22":       "/elements/books/bookV/propositions/propV22/",
        "X.6":        "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX6/",
        "X.6.Cor":    "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX6/#cor",
        "X.9":        "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX9/",
        "X.36":       "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX36/"
    });
</script>
</figure>

Set out any rational straight line {E}, and let it be contrived that {D} is to {AB} as the square on {E} is to the square on {FG}. Then the square on {E} is commensurable with the square on {FG}.  And {E} is rational, therefore {FG} is also rational. [!just X.6.Cor; X.6]

Now, since {D} does not have to {AB} the ratio which a square number has to a square number, neither does the square on {E} have to the square on {FG} the ratio which a square number has to a square number, therefore {E} is incommensurable in length with {FG}. [!just X.9]

Again, let it be contrived that {BA} is to {AC} as the square on {FG} is to the square on {GH}. Then the square on {FG} is commensurable with the square on {HG}. [!just X.6.Cor; X.6]

Therefore the square on {HG} is rational. Therefore {HG} is rational. And, since {BA} does not have to {AC} the ratio which a square number has to a square number, neither does the square on {FG} have to the square on {GH} the ratio which a square number has to a square number, therefore {FG} is incommensurable in length with {GH}. [!just X.9]

Therefore {FG} and {GH} are rational straight lines commensurable in square only. Therefore {FH} is binomial. [!just X.36]

It is next to be proved that it is also a sixth binomial straight line.

Since {D} is to {AB} as the square on {E} is to the square on {FG}, and also {BA} is to {AC} as the square on {FG} is to the square on {GH}, therefore, *ex aequali*, {D} is to {AC} as the square on {E} is to the square on {GH}. [!just V.22]

But {D} does not have to {AC} the ratio which a square number has to a square number, therefore neither does the square on {E} have to the square on {GH} the ratio which a square number has to a square number, therefore {E} is incommensurable in length with {GH}. [!just X.9]

But it was also proved incommensurable with {FG}, therefore each of the straight lines {FG} and {GH} is incommensurable in length with {E}.

And, since {BA} is to {AC} as the square on {FG} is to the square on {GH}, therefore the square on {FG} is greater than the square on {GH}.

Let then the sum of the squares on {GH} and *K* equal the square on {FG}.  Then, in conversion, {AB} is to {BC} as the square on {FG} is to the square on *K*. [!just V.19.Cor]

But {AB} does not have to {BC} the ratio which a square number has to a square number, so that neither does the square on {FG} have to the square on *K* the ratio which a square number has to a square number.

Therefore {FG} is incommensurable in length with *A*. Therefore the square on {FG} is greater than the square on {GH} by the square on a straight line incommensurable with {FG}. [!just X.9]

And {FG} and {GH} are rational straight lines commensurable in square only, and neither of them is commensurable in length with the rational straight line {E} set out.

Therefore {FH} is a sixth binomial straight line.

<div class="qed">Q.E.D.</div>
